<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>MyPinata – App Support</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta
    name="description"
    content="Support page for the MyPinata app – create and manage product sampling events."
  />
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f9fafb;
      --card-bg: #ffffff;
      --text: #111827;
      --muted: #6b7280;
      --accent: #facc15;
      --accent-dark: #d4af0f;
      --border: #e5e7eb;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI",
        sans-serif;
      background-color: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .page {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 3rem;
    }

    header {
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    header h1 {
      margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    header p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .card {
      background-color: var(--card-bg);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.04);
    }

    .card h2 {
      margin-top: 0;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background-color: rgba(250, 204, 21, 0.12);
      color: #92400e;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }

    .cta-box {
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
      padding-left: 1rem;
      margin-top: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    ul {
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
      margin: 0.4rem 0 0.6rem;
    }

    li {
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }

    .contact-list {
      list-style: none;
      padding-left: 0;
    }

    .contact-list li {
      margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    }

    a {
      color: #2563eb;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .btn {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 0.9rem;
      padding: 0.55rem 1.2rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #1f2933;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent-dark);
    }

    .btn:hover {
      background: var(--accent-dark);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .faq-item {
      margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
    }

    .faq-item h3 {
      margin: 0 0 0.15rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .small {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    footer {
      margin-top: 2rem;
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    @media (min-width: 768px) {
      .card {
        padding: 2rem 2rem;
      }

      header h1 {
        font-size: 2.3rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="page">
    <header>
      <h1>MyPinata – App Support</h1>
      <p>
        Help and support for brands, field teams, and coordinators using the
        MyPinata sampling events app.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="card">
      <span class="badge">About the App</span>
      <h2>What is MyPinata?</h2>
      <p>
        MyPinata is a mobile app designed to help brands and field teams
        <strong>create, schedule, and manage product sampling events</strong>.
        It’s ideal for sampling new food, beverages, and other consumer
        products in stores, events, or pop-ups.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Create sampling events with a simple form.</li>
        <li>Assign locations, dates, and products to each event.</li>
        <li>Track event details and status in one place.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cta-box">
        If you’re new to MyPinata, start by creating your first event inside the
        app and adding a product, date, time, and location.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <span class="badge">Getting Started</span>
      <h2>How to Use MyPinata</h2>
      <ol class="small">
        <li>Download and install the MyPinata app from the App Store.</li>
        <li>Sign in with the credentials provided by your company or program lead.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>“Create Event”</strong> to set up a new sampling event.</li>
        <li>Enter event name, date, time, and location.</li>
        <li>Add the products you’ll be sampling (e.g., new beverages or food items).</li>
        <li>Save the event and use the event list to review or update details.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="small">
        If you don’t see any events, your account may not be linked to a
        program yet. Please contact your manager or support.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <span class="badge">FAQ</span>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do I need an account to use the app?</h3>
        <p class="small">
          Yes. MyPinata is typically used by brands, agencies, or teams running
          sampling programs. Your administrator or manager will provide your
          login information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>I can’t log in. What should I do?</h3>
        <p class="small">
          Double-check your email and password, including capitalization. If you
          still can’t sign in, contact support so we can verify your account and
          reset your access if needed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>My events are not showing up.</h3>
        <p class="small">
          Make sure you’re signed in with the correct account. If events are
          still missing, your account might not be assigned to any active
          programs or locations. Please contact your manager or support with
          your name and company.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How do I edit or cancel an event?</h3>
        <p class="small">
          Open the event from the main list, then use the edit options provided
          inside the app. If you don’t see edit controls, changes may need to be
          handled by your program administrator.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Which devices are supported?</h3>
        <p class="small">
          MyPinata is designed for iOS devices running a recent version of iOS.
          For the best experience, keep your device and the app updated to the
          latest version.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <span class="badge">Contact</span>
      <h2>Need More Help?</h2>
      <p class="small">
        If you’re experiencing an issue that isn’t covered above, please reach
        out with as much detail as possible:
      </p>
      <ul class="contact-list small">
        <li>
          <strong>Email:</strong>
          <a href="mailto:mypinata@mypinata.com">mypinata@mypinata.com</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Include:</strong> your name, company, device model, iOS
          version, and a brief description of the issue.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:mypinata@mypinata.com">Contact Support</a>
    </section>

    <footer>
      &copy; 2025 MyPinata. All rights reserved.
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
